  <body>
    <!-- HERO — the one cinematic moment -->
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-media" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ribbon">
        <span class="ribbon-mark">LDI</span>
        <span class="ribbon-name">Lithium Dreams · Glasshouse Systems Studio</span>
        <span class="ribbon-tag">Private proposal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-eyebrow">Prepared for Jay Robertson · Robertson Real Estate</div>
        <h1>A growth system, built around <em>your business.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">You've built something real. This is about making it work harder for you — on your terms.</p>
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span>Prepared by <b>John Burroughs</b></span>
          <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Lithium Dreams · Glasshouse</span>
          <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>2026-09-14</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="scroll-cue" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bar"></span>Scroll</div>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap">

      <!-- PERSONAL NOTE -->
      <section>
        <div class="note">
          <p>Jay — good running into you at the gas station today. Hope the tire cooperated. It's always good to catch up and give each other a hard time. It also got me thinking on the drive home, so I spent a little time since with your website and your business and put this together — something concrete for us to talk through when we sit down.</p>
          <p>First, the important part: <strong>you've built something real.</strong> Robertson Real Estate has a modern site, a genuine MLS search, a strong team, and a niche — farms and land — that most agencies in this part of the state don't take seriously. This isn't about fixing anything that's broken. It's about taking a good foundation and making it work harder: responding to every lead the moment it comes in, being the obvious online authority on Southeast Iowa farm and land, and giving your four agents their time back.</p>
          <p>That's the kind of work I do. I take a business's own strengths and its own goals, and I build the systems and technology around <em>them</em> — not a product I'm trying to sell you. This capability is the product of years of building and refining real operational systems; what follows is that work, pointed at Robertson Real Estate.</p>
          <p>And I'll be straight with you: I'd rather do this for someone local. You're building something in the same community I'm from — keeping that kind of work close to home, between two people who'll actually run into each other again, matters to me.</p>
          <p class="signoff">Here's how I see it. — John</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
      <section>
        <div class="summary">
          <div class="sec-eyebrow">In Short</div>
          <h2>The opportunity is <em>conversion</em>, not repair.</h2>
          <p class="muted">Robertson Real Estate runs a capable, modern website with full MLS search on a solid platform. The opportunity isn't technical repair — it's turning interest you're <em>already getting</em> into clients you're not yet closing.</p>
          <p class="muted">Three things move the needle most: <strong>(1)</strong> responding to every website lead instantly, day or night; <strong>(2)</strong> turning your farm-and-land expertise into a visible online authority that pulls in the buyers and sellers competitors ignore; and <strong>(3)</strong> taking the repetitive marketing and paperwork off your team's plate so they can sell.</p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">It's a partnership, not a hand-off. A monthly plan keeps the tools tuned and the content coming — and when something isn't working, you call me. You're never left spinning your wheels.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- WHAT I SEE -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">What I See in Your Business</div>
        <h2>A strong foundation — with room to work harder.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">Credit where it's due. You already have the pieces most agencies struggle to get right:</p>
        <div class="strengths">
          <div class="strength"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>A modern, mobile-friendly site with real MLS search</b><span>Buyers can find and browse listings — the hard part is done.</span></div></div>
          <div class="strength"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Full lead capture — Dream Home Finder, market analysis, buyer accounts</b><span>The plumbing to capture interest is in place.</span></div></div>
          <div class="strength"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>A real team of four across a wide SE Iowa footprint</b><span>The capacity to grow into more volume.</span></div></div>
          <div class="strength"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Farms · Residential · Commercial — a genuine niche</b><span>The farm-and-land angle is your single biggest differentiator.</span></div></div>
        </div>

        <p class="lead-p" style="margin-top:34px;">And here's where the growth is — each one a place where a little technology turns interest into clients:</p>
        <div class="levers">
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">1</div><div>
            <h3>Respond to every lead in minutes, not hours</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>You've already got the hard part — real capture forms (Dream Home Finder, market analysis, buyer accounts). The interest is coming in.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>But a form that arrives at 9pm waits until someone's free the next morning. In real estate the first agent to reply usually gets the client — so a lead that sat overnight has often already called the next name on their list. Slow reply → lost first-mover → a client who was yours to win closes with someone else.</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>Every inquiry gets an <b>instant, personal reply</b> and routes to the right agent automatically — Tuesday lunch or Sunday midnight, it doesn't matter.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">2</div><div>
            <h3>Answer the question that comes after hours</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>Outside those forms, a visitor with a quick question — "do you handle land?", "is this one still available?" — has nowhere to ask once the office is closed.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>Nobody fills out a form to ask one thing. A question with no answer just becomes a closed tab — they leave, and you never knew they were there. No answer → no capture → a lead that never lands on your books at all.</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>A friendly assistant on the site answers the common questions, helps people find the right listing, and <b>quietly captures who they are</b> — then hands a warm lead to the right agent.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">3</div><div>
            <h3>Own the farm &amp; land conversation online</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>The site lists Farms, Residential, and Commercial side by side — but farm and land, your real edge, reads as one tab of three rather than the headline.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>The landowner Googling "sell my farm ground in SE Iowa," or the out-of-area buyer researching tillable acres and CSR2, is exactly the high-value client who starts online — and right now they don't find a clear expert, so they land on whoever happened to rank. Invisible online → the ag search traffic goes to a generalist → your best differentiator earns you nothing.</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>Become <b>the obvious name</b> for Southeast Iowa farm and land online — the guides, the valuations, and the plain-English answers a landowner is actually searching for.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">4</div><div>
            <h3>A site that looks as current as your business is</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>A few honest first-impression things: the news and blog posts stop in 2024, the contact form still lists a fax number, and the photography and layout are the clean-but-generic look a lot of agency sites share — professional, but it could be almost any office.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>A first-time visitor forms a snap judgment in seconds. "Last posted 2024" and a fax line quietly read as <i>"is this place still active?"</i> — even when you're busier than ever — and a template look says "same as everyone else." Dated first impression → less trust before they've met you → the call goes to whoever looked sharper. (Stale content slips you down in search, too.)</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>Regular local content in your voice, current details, and a look that feels like <b>Robertson specifically</b> — so the site finally matches the quality of the work you actually do.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">5</div><div>
            <h3>Give your agents their time back</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>Every listing means a write-up, the social posts, a just-listed / just-sold graphic, the newsletter — built by hand, four agents deep.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>Hours spent on copy-and-paste marketing are hours not spent with clients — and when everyone's slammed, the marketing is the first thing skipped or rushed. Manual busywork → less selling time and thinner marketing → fewer touches on the listings that actually pay you.</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>The routine marketing <b>produces itself</b> from the listing details — your team reviews and approves in minutes instead of starting from a blank page.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="lever"><div class="lever-num">6</div><div>
            <h3>Turn browsers into sellers, not just buyers</h3>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label noticed">Noticed</span>The site is built for buyers browsing listings; there's no real front door for an owner just wondering what their home — or their ground — is worth.</p>
            <p class="beat"><span class="beat-label leads">Where it leads</span>Sellers are the higher-value side of the business, but the curious owner who isn't ready to call an agent yet has no low-pressure way in — so they drift off and eventually list with whoever asked first. No seller path → no early capture → the listing goes to a competitor.</p>
            <p class="beat opp"><span class="beat-label opp">The opportunity</span>A simple <b>"what's my property (or farm) worth"</b> experience that turns a curious owner into a name in your pipeline — and a listing appointment down the road.</p>
          </div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- THE IDEA -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">The Idea</div>
        <h2>A <em>system</em>, not a gadget.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">The point isn't to bolt on a chatbot and call it done. It's one simple, connected spine that every lead travels along:</p>
        <div class="spine">
          <div class="stage">
            <div class="label">Capture</div>
            <p>An assistant on your site greets every visitor, answers questions, and captures interest.</p>
            <div class="plain">Never miss an inquiry.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage">
            <div class="label">Convert</div>
            <p>That lead gets an instant reply, a quick qualification, and goes to the right agent — plus a seller-side path for owners weighing a sale.</p>
            <div class="plain">Be the first to respond, every time.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage">
            <div class="label">Compound</div>
            <p>Your listings market themselves, and local + farm/land content builds authority that grows your traffic month over month.</p>
            <div class="plain">The system gets stronger the longer it runs.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:18px;">Behind it, one simple dashboard shows you every lead, where it came from, and where it stands — the same kind of command center I run my own operation from.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- DEMO -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">See It in Action</div>
        <h2>Your AI Front Desk — try it.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">This is a working taste of the "Capture" piece: a 24/7 assistant on your website. Ask it something a buyer or seller might, or tap a question below.</p>
        <div class="demo-frame">
          <div class="demo-head">
            <div class="t"><b>Robertson Real Estate — Front Desk</b><span>A demonstration of the AI assistant</span></div>
            <span class="demo-badge">Demo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chat" id="chat">
            <div class="chat-bar">
              <div class="chat-av">R</div>
              <div class="who"><b>Robertson Real Estate</b><span>Online now</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="chat-log" id="chatLog"></div>
            <div class="chips" id="chatChips"></div>
            <form class="chat-input" id="chatForm" autocomplete="off">
              <input id="chatInput" type="text" placeholder="Type your question…" aria-label="Message" />
              <button type="submit">Send</button>
            </form>
          </div>
          <p class="print-only" style="color:var(--muted);text-align:center;margin:16px 0 0;">[ Live AI Front Desk demonstration — visit the online proposal to try it. It answers buyer and seller questions 24/7, surfaces listings conversationally, highlights your farm &amp; land expertise, and captures each visitor's name and number for your team. ]</p>
          <p class="demo-caption">Illustrative responses for demonstration. Your live version connects to your real listings, your team, and your CRM.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- MODULES -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">What We Could Build</div>
        <h2>Pick what fits.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">À la carte, on purpose. You don't have to take all of it, and not all at once. Start with what would help you most.</p>
        <div class="modules">
          <div class="module"><div class="mtitle"><b>AI Front Desk</b></div><p>A 24/7 assistant on your site — answers buyer and seller questions, helps people find listings, captures name and intent, hands off to the right agent.</p></div>
          <div class="module"><div class="mtitle"><b>Speed-to-Lead</b></div><p>Every new lead gets an instant, personalized reply and is routed automatically to Jay, Greyson, Brad, or Eva — with optional friendly follow-ups.</p></div>
          <div class="module"><div class="mtitle"><b>Listing Content Studio</b></div><p>Feed in the address, photos, and facts → out comes a polished listing description, "just listed / just sold / open house" posts and graphics, and a property flyer.</p></div>
          <div class="module"><div class="mtitle"><b>Local Authority Engine</b></div><p>Neighborhood and town guides, monthly county market updates, a revived blog, and a fixed, current news feed — written for you, approved by you.</p></div>
          <div class="module star"><div class="mtitle"><b>Farm, Land &amp; Recreation Intelligence</b><span class="starmark">Your edge</span></div><p>Farmland and recreational/hunting-land guides, land-value and CSR2 explainers, aerial and topo listing detail, a "sell your farm, land, or hunting ground" funnel, and SE-Iowa ag and commercial intel — positioning Robertson as the regional land expert.</p></div>
          <div class="module"><div class="mtitle"><b>Seller Magnet</b></div><p>Branded, easy-to-read home and farm value reports, and a "what's it worth" experience that captures seller leads — the higher-value side of the business.</p></div>
          <div class="module" style="grid-column:1/-1;"><div class="mtitle"><b>Website Polish</b></div><p>Rewriting the stock website copy in your voice, an authentic About/story, refreshed testimonials, and tidying small dated details.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FARM & LAND HIGHLIGHT -->
      <section>
        <div class="highlight">
          <div class="sec-eyebrow">The Angle I Keep Coming Back To</div>
          <h2>Own the <em>land</em> conversation in Southeast Iowa.</h2>
          <p>Every agency in the area sells houses. Far fewer can speak credibly about ag land — valuation, tillable acres, CSR2, farm sales, 1031 exchanges, the things a landowner actually cares about. You already do this. Almost none of it shows up online, where the search traffic and the out-of-area buyers are.</p>
          <p>If we did nothing else, making Robertson the obvious online authority on Southeast Iowa land would likely be the highest-return move on this whole page. It's a moat you already own and just haven't planted a flag on yet.</p>

          <hr class="rule" />
          <p class="subhead">And there's a second kind of land you're sitting on.</p>
          <p>Iowa is one of the top trophy-whitetail states in the country — third in the nation for record-book bucks. The nonresident deer tag is a lottery most applicants <em>lose</em>, so serious hunters buy ground here to guarantee their access. That buyer isn't after tillable acres; they want timber, a creek bottom, a ridge, a gully — the recreational ground that's easy to treat as leftover. And there's real money in it: hunting and recreational parcels routinely sell at a premium over bare cropland.</p>
          <p>This isn't a hunch — it's a proven playbook. <b style="color:#fff;">Whitetail Properties</b> sells land across 26 states and runs its own show on the Sportsman Channel; <b style="color:#fff;">Mossy Oak Properties</b> operates 100-plus franchised land offices. Closer to home, <b style="color:#fff;">LandGuys</b> — out of Ottumwa, about an hour from you — built its whole reputation on outdoor-TV and magazine features for recreational ground. And on <b style="color:#fff;">LandWatch</b>, the site these buyers actually search, there are tens of thousands of hunting-land listings nationwide. The demand and the playbook are established — nobody's run it in your backyard yet. Listing recreational ground the way that buyer searches — aerials, topography, timber and water, deer country — with real content behind it could open a buyer pool most local agencies never touch. <b style="color:#fff;">You know this ground far better than I do — I'd want your read on whether it's worth chasing.</b></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- HOW WE'D WORK -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">How We'd Work Together</div>
        <h2>Low-risk, and proven before it scales.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">I don't believe in turning on everything at once and hoping.</p>
        <div class="phases">
          <div class="phase"><div class="pn">1</div><div>
            <h3>Talk it through</h3>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">We sit down, I learn how leads actually flow through your shop today, and we pick the one or two things worth doing first.</p>
            <p class="why">Free. Relationship first — I want to build the right thing, not the biggest thing.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="phase"><div class="pn">2</div><div>
            <h3>A small, real pilot</h3>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">We stand up the first piece — likely the Front Desk plus instant lead response — and run it with one of your agents.</p>
            <p class="why">You see it working on real leads before the whole team commits.</p>
          </div></div>
          <div class="phase"><div class="pn">3</div><div>
            <h3>Grow what works</h3>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">Once the pilot proves out, we roll it to the full team and add the pieces that compound — content, the farm/land authority, the seller side.</p>
            <p class="why">You're only ever expanding things you've already seen work.</p>
          </div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="partner">
          <p><strong>And it's a partnership, not a drop-off.</strong> Everything we build is covered by a simple monthly plan: the tools stay tuned, the content keeps coming on a steady cadence, and — this part matters — <strong>when you or your team get stuck or want a change, you reach out to me directly.</strong> No ticket queue, no waiting, no spinning your wheels on something technical.</p>
          <p><strong>And because it's me, not a big agency, everything moves faster.</strong> A change you want this week gets made this week — not queued behind a hundred other clients' tickets. When something breaks or isn't quite landing, I can usually track it down and fix it the same day, because there's no layer of account managers or support tiers between you and the person who actually built the thing. No corporate overhead to move around is exactly why a small shop like mine turns work around in a fraction of the time a larger company can.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:0;">That's the whole point of working with a person instead of a piece of software.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- INVESTMENT -->
      <section>
        <div class="sec-eyebrow">Investment</div>
        <h2>Two simple parts.</h2>
        <p class="lead-p">A one-time <strong>setup</strong> for each piece we build, and a <strong>monthly plan</strong> that keeps it running and keeps me on call. Start with whatever helps most and grow as it pays for itself — no big commitment up front, and the setup doesn't have to be a lump sum: we can spread it out or fold it into the monthly.</p>

        <div class="pilot">
          <div class="tag">Start here — a low-risk pilot</div>
          <h3>AI Front Desk + instant lead response</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">Run with one of your agents first, so you see it working on real leads before the whole team commits.</p>
          <div class="nums">
            <div><span>One-time setup</span><b>$2,500 – 3,500</b></div>
            <div><span>Monthly</span><b>from $300</b> <span style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;">(Essentials plan)</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tiers">
          <div class="tier">
            <div class="tname">Essentials</div>
            <div class="price">$300<small>/mo &amp; up</small></div>
            <p>Everything stays running and updated, small tweaks as needed, a monthly check-in — and you can reach me directly whenever you or your team get stuck.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier rec">
            <div class="rec-badge">Recommended</div>
            <div class="tname">Growth</div>
            <div class="price">$650<small>/mo &amp; up</small></div>
            <p>Essentials, plus a steady stream of fresh content, monthly reporting on your leads, and ongoing tuning to keep improving results.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier">
            <div class="tname">Partner</div>
            <div class="price">$1,200<small>/mo &amp; up</small></div>
            <p>Growth, plus full content and search work, the farm &amp; land authority engine running in full, and quarterly strategy sessions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bundle">
          <h3>The full Growth System — if you ever want the whole thing</h3>
          <p class="muted">Most people start with one piece and grow. But if you'd rather build the whole system at once, the founder's rate for everything is <strong><span class="price">$5,000 – 7,000</span></strong> — well under what the pieces total separately, and a fraction of the $20,000-plus it costs to assemble from separate vendors. <strong>And you'd never write a check that size.</strong> We can spread the setup across your first year — roughly $400–580 a month on top of your plan — or fold it in however works for your cash flow. I scope it to your budget, not the other way around.</p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>Why the founder's rate:</strong> you'd be my first client here — and we're both local, we already know each other, and I'd rather prove this works for a neighbor than maximize an invoice. It's genuine: offered for your honest feedback as we build and, if you're happy, your okay to point to Robertson as an example of my work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vcompare">
          <h3>What this replaces — and what it would cost elsewhere</h3>
          <p class="muted">You're not choosing between me and nothing. You're choosing between me and the corporate tools most agencies rent — which cost more every month, tie you to a contract, and give you a support queue instead of a person who picks up.</p>
          <div class="vwrap">
            <table class="vtable">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>What you want to do</th><th>The usual route (rented)</th><th>With me (built for you)</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td class="want">Instant lead capture &amp; auto-response</td>
                  <td class="usual">A realtor lead platform like <b>Ylopo</b> — commonly <b>$400–500/mo</b>, typically on an annual contract, and you're renting the tool on their terms</td>
                  <td class="mine">Built into your own site and folded into your monthly plan — month-to-month, and when you need something you <b>call me</b></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="want">Full team lead &amp; follow-up platform</td>
                  <td class="usual">A team platform like <b>CINC</b> — commonly <b>$900–1,500+/mo</b>, scales up as you add agents, contract lock-in</td>
                  <td class="mine">Included in your plan — <b>doesn't cost more as your team grows</b>, and built around how Jay, Greyson, Brad and Eva actually work</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="want">Chatbot + website work + lead automation</td>
                  <td class="usual">Three separate vendors — often <b>$20,000+</b> to stand up, and three companies to manage and reconcile</td>
                  <td class="mine">One bundled founder's rate of <b>$5,000–7,000</b> — one person who built all of it and stands behind it</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="want">Ongoing content + local SEO</td>
                  <td class="usual">A marketing-agency retainer — commonly <b>$1,000–3,000/mo</b>, written by someone who's never met your market</td>
                  <td class="mine">Included in the Growth or Partner plan — in your voice, about your towns, <b>approved by you</b> before it posts</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="compare">You know the commission on a typical sale here far better than I do — run it against these numbers. For most shops, <b style="font-style:normal;color:var(--green);">one or two extra closings a year covers the entire system</b>, and everything past that is upside. What the corporate tools rent you, this you own.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="assurances">
          <h3>How this works, in plain English</h3>
          <div class="asrow"><span class="ascheck">✓</span><div><b>We measure it.</b> Every month you get a simple scorecard — how fast leads got answered, how many came in, how many turned into real conversations. You see exactly what you're paying for, in numbers, not adjectives.</div></div>
          <div class="asrow"><span class="ascheck">✓</span><div><b>No lock-in.</b> The monthly is month-to-month — cancel any time, no long contract. And what we build for you, you keep.</div></div>
          <div class="asrow"><span class="ascheck">✓</span><div><b>Fair-housing safe.</b> Anything that talks to your leads is built to stay on the right side of fair-housing rules — no steering, no answering the questions an agent legally shouldn't. I handle that so you never have to worry about it.</div></div>
          <div class="asrow"><span class="ascheck">✓</span><div><b>You own it.</b> It lives on your own site and in your own accounts — not rented from a platform that keeps everything the day you stop paying.</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CLOSE -->
      <section>
        <div class="close-block">
          <div class="sec-eyebrow">A Starting Point</div>
          <h2>This is the opening of a <em>conversation</em>.</h2>
          <p class="muted">Jay, everything above is my read from the outside. You know your business, your customers, and this market far better than I do — so treat this as a starting point, not a pitch to accept or decline.</p>
          <p class="muted">When we meet, the most useful thing you can tell me is what's actually been nagging at you — where you feel you're losing time, or losing clients, or wishing the website did more. We build from <em>there</em>. If a piece here doesn't fit how you work, we drop it. If there's something not here that you've wanted, that's exactly what I want to hear.</p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">I'm genuinely excited about the possibility of working together. Let's find the version of this that's right for Robertson.</p>
          <p class="signoff">— John</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer>
        <div class="foot">
          <span><b>John Burroughs</b></span>
          <span>Lithium Dreams · Glasshouse Systems Studio</span>
          <span>lithium-dreams.com/work</span>
          <span>Prepared 2026-09-14 · for Robertson Real Estate</span>
        </div>
      </footer>

    </div>

    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var log = document.getElementById('chatLog');
        var chipBar = document.getElementById('chatChips');
        var form = document.getElementById('chatForm');
        var input = document.getElementById('chatInput');
        var awaitingContact = false;

        function scroll() { log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight; }

        function addMsg(text, who) {
          var d = document.createElement('div');
          d.className = 'msg ' + who;
          d.textContent = text;
          log.appendChild(d);
          scroll();
        }

        function setChips(items) {
          chipBar.innerHTML = '';
          (items || []).forEach(function (c) {
            var b = document.createElement('button');
            b.type = 'button';
            b.className = 'chip';
            b.textContent = c.label;
            b.addEventListener('click', function () { handleUser(c.label, c.key); });
            chipBar.appendChild(b);
          });
        }

        function typing(done) {
          var t = document.createElement('div');
          t.className = 'typing';
          t.innerHTML = '<i></i><i></i><i></i>';
          log.appendChild(t);
          scroll();
          setTimeout(function () { t.remove(); done(); }, 850);
        }

        function botSay(text, chips) {
          typing(function () {
            addMsg(text, 'bot');
            if (chips !== undefined) setChips(chips);
          });
        }

        var flows = {
          farm: {
            reply: "Absolutely — farm and land is one of our specialties. We handle tillable ground, pasture, recreational land, and full farm sales across Southeast Iowa, from Louisa and Muscatine counties out to Johnson and Washington. Are you looking to buy land, or thinking about selling a farm you own?",
            chips: [
              { label: "I want to sell my farm", key: "sell" },
              { label: "Show me land for sale", key: "listings" },
              { label: "What's my land worth?", key: "worth" }
            ]
          },
          worth: {
            reply: "Happy to help you find out. We put together a real market analysis from recent comparable sales in your area — not just an automated guess. If you share your property address, I can have one of our agents prepare a free, no-obligation valuation. Want me to set that up?",
            chips: [
              { label: "Yes, have someone reach out", key: "capture" },
              { label: "Tell me about your team", key: "agent" }
            ]
          },
          listings: {
            reply: "You bet — we've got active listings across Columbus Junction and the surrounding counties, updated daily from the MLS. What are you looking for — a home, farm/land, or commercial? And any must-haves, like acreage or number of bedrooms?",
            chips: [
              { label: "Homes for sale", key: "homes" },
              { label: "Acreage / land", key: "farm" },
              { label: "Commercial property", key: "commercial" }
            ]
          },
          homes: {
            reply: "Great — I can pull homes that match what you're after and set you up with new-listing alerts so you're first to know. Tell me your price range and the area you're focused on, and I'll have an agent send over a curated list. Want me to have someone reach out?",
            chips: [ { label: "Yes, have someone reach out", key: "capture" } ]
          },
          commercial: {
            reply: "We handle commercial and investment property across the region too — retail, office, land for development, and more. Let me connect you with the right person on our team who knows the local commercial market. Shall I have them get in touch?",
            chips: [ { label: "Yes, please", key: "capture" } ]
          },
          sell: {
            reply: "That's exactly what we're here for. Whether it's a home, a farm, or a commercial building, we'll walk you through pricing, prep, and marketing — and selling farm or land is a particular strength of ours. Want me to have Jay Robertson give you a call to talk it through?",
            chips: [ { label: "Yes, have Jay call me", key: "capture" } ]
          },
          agent: {
            reply: "Of course. Our team is Jay Robertson, Greyson Conlon, Brad Akers, and Eva Garcia — someone's always glad to help. If you leave your name and the best number to reach you, I'll make sure the right person gets back to you quickly.",
            chips: [ { label: "Okay — here's my info", key: "capture" } ]
          },
          hours: {
            reply: "Our office is in Columbus Junction and you can reach the team at 319-728-8891. But this front desk is open around the clock — so ask me anything, day or night, and I'll help or pass you to the right person.",
            chips: [
              { label: "Show me listings", key: "listings" },
              { label: "Talk to an agent", key: "agent" }
            ]
          },
          capture: {
            reply: "Wonderful. What's the best name and number (or email) to reach you? I'll pass it straight to the team.",
            capture: true
          }
        };

        function matchFree(text) {
          var t = text.toLowerCase();
          if (/(farm|land|acre|ag |ground|tillable|pasture|csr)/.test(t)) return 'farm';
          if (/(worth|value|apprais|how much|market analysis|cma)/.test(t)) return 'worth';
          if (/(sell|selling|list my|put.*market)/.test(t)) return 'sell';
          if (/(listing|for sale|buy|browse|search|home|house)/.test(t)) return 'listings';
          if (/(commercial|office|retail|investment)/.test(t)) return 'commercial';
          if (/(agent|talk|call|speak|contact|reach|person|human)/.test(t)) return 'agent';
          if (/(hour|open|phone|number|address|where|located)/.test(t)) return 'hours';
          return null;
        }

        function handleUser(text, key) {
          addMsg(text, 'user');
          setChips([]);

          if (awaitingContact) {
            awaitingContact = false;
            botSay("Perfect — I've passed that along to the team, and someone will reach out to you shortly. Is there anything else I can help with in the meantime?", [
              { label: "Show me listings", key: "listings" },
              { label: "Tell me about farm & land", key: "farm" }
            ]);
            return;
          }

          var flow = key ? flows[key] : null;
          if (!flow) { var m = matchFree(text); flow = m ? flows[m] : null; }

          if (!flow) {
            botSay("Good question — let me get you to the right person on our team who can help with that. In the meantime, is there something specific you're looking for?", [
              { label: "Farm & land", key: "farm" },
              { label: "What's my home worth?", key: "worth" },
              { label: "Talk to an agent", key: "agent" }
            ]);
            return;
          }

          if (flow.capture) { awaitingContact = true; botSay(flow.reply, []); return; }
          botSay(flow.reply, flow.chips);
        }

        form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          var v = input.value.trim();
          if (!v) return;
          input.value = '';
          handleUser(v, null);
        });

        // Opening
        setTimeout(function () {
          botSay("Hi there! Welcome to Robertson Real Estate. I can help you find listings, get a home or land valuation, or connect you with one of our agents. What brings you in today?", [
            { label: "Do you handle farm & land?", key: "farm" },
            { label: "What's my home worth?", key: "worth" },
            { label: "Show me listings", key: "listings" },
            { label: "I want to sell", key: "sell" }
          ]);
        }, 400);
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
